# mirai-station — runtime artifacts that regenerate on the mini

# venv lives outside the plugin tree, but be defensive
.venv/
venv/

# python build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# pytest
.pytest_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Logs & rolling state — written on the mini, never synced from main.
# 2026-07-10: the whole state/ tree is runtime data (5-min diaries, lance DB,
# lob ticks, ~158MB and churning) — machine-local, never versioned.
state/
state/logs/

# Per-skill caches and run history that regenerate from live data
skills/*/cache/
skills/*/logs/
skills/iv-viability/cache/
skills/mirai-left-eye/logs/

# The built phone shell, served from the station so a phone can install it over
# the same front door. It is the one file under static/ that contains the
# station password in plain text, so it must never be committable — the scrub
# refuses a TRACKED apk, but an untracked one sitting in `git status` is an
# invitation, and mirai-mobile/.gitignore only reaches its own directory.
runtime/viewstation/static/m/*.apk

# The scanner's rolling intraday state. It is runtime data like everything under
# state/ — hunter.load_state() returns a fresh day when the file is absent and
# resets it at 09:30 ET anyway — but it lived here, beside the code, and so was
# tracked by accident rather than by decision. What it holds is a live signal:
# which direction armed, on which instrument, at which second. Four commits
# published one before 2026-09-04, and with development moving to the public
# repo a `git commit -a` would publish today's.
skills/mirai-left-eye/state.json
